WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.860
The four jobs of a manager.

2
00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:10.673
Here is the idea in one sentence: being a manager is not a title, it is four jobs you do every week.

3
00:00:10.723 --> 00:00:12.783
Job one: get the work done.

4
00:00:12.833 --> 00:00:21.378
Decide what matters, tell people what is expected, check work before it is due, and fix problems at the cause.

5
00:00:21.428 --> 00:00:24.035
Job two: take care of your people.

6
00:00:24.085 --> 00:00:31.301
Listen and help, grow them, thank them for specific work, and trust them with real decisions.

7
00:00:31.351 --> 00:00:33.645
Job three: make things better.

8
00:00:33.695 --> 00:00:40.756
Explain the why behind changes, describe where the team is going, let people try new ideas,

9
00:00:40.806 --> 00:00:47.319
and look back after big work. Job four: connect your team to the rest of Vanderbilt.

10
00:00:47.369 --> 00:00:55.289
Know the people your team depends on, watch for what is coming, and speak up for your team with facts.

11
00:00:55.339 --> 00:00:57.477
Every manager does all four.

12
00:00:57.527 --> 00:01:04.353
Most weeks need one of them more than the others, and part of the job is noticing which.

13
00:01:04.403 --> 00:01:08.104
These four jobs come from research by Gary Yukl.

14
00:01:08.154 --> 00:01:15.292
Vanderbilt uses them as a guide, and the survey you will receive asks about the same habits.

15
00:01:15.342 --> 00:01:20.293
Now tap each card on the page to see the habits inside each job.

